Spec rev 140 ("Permissions and tasks") changes what two invariant tests
encode. Apply from the repository root with `git apply` this file; see
decisions/2026-11-10-permissions-asks.md.

inv4_taint::private_data_sent_to_a_wider_audience_asks encodes the audience
ask (private data to a wider audience, without untrusted input), which rev 140
deletes: only private data going to a new destination after untrusted input
asks (case 3). The test passes today only because the scripted model cannot
answer Auto Review. Its replacement makes the same post after an untrusted
page, and checks the card offers neither a task-wide Allow nor Allow always.

inv7_verify::a_criterion_without_a_check_goes_to_the_person_for_review sends
criteria to the person, an ask outside the four. Rev 140: "That checking is
internal: the person sees the result, not criteria or contracts." The kernel
path is removed; the replacement checks the task completes, nothing is put to
the person, and the criterion is recorded as unconfirmed.

The contract-change hunk of docs/proposals/invariant-tests-tightened.patch
(criteria_changed_after_work_begins_need_an_approved_contract_change) is
obsolete: rev 140 has no contract change put to the person; a change after
the work began is refused (tests/scratch/tests/contract_freeze.rs).

